<!--
license:CC0-1.0

Technics SX-KN7000 floppy disks.

User-data and sound/style-library disks for the KN7000, as self-extracting PC
archives that write their payload onto a blank FAT12 HD diskette: the factory
"Initial Data" / "Custom Data" sets the instrument installs on a front-panel data
load (populating the custom-data flash IC21 and the battery-backed user memory),
plus add-on sound, style and SD-converter library disks.  Physical diskettes are
known to exist; who prepared or distributed them is unclear (not necessarily
official releases).  No original diskette has been dumped, so these images are
faithful reconstructions built from the archives' own files, which a dump of an
original could supersede.
-->
